        <AbbreviatedIRI>obo:OBI_0000425</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">A mean calculation which has averaging objective is a descriptive statistics calculation in which the mean is calculated by taking the sum of all of the observations in a data set divided by the total number of observations. It gives a measure of the &apos;center of gravity&apos; for the data set. It is also known as the first moment.</Literal>
